Because you don't otherwise have MR yet, I'd
tend to lean in the direction of wielding MB most
of the time even if it does less damage than your
other weapon options (in this case, none).  MR is
extremely nice to have and prevents many different
kinds of sudden death, as well as numerous lesser
annoyances.

Whether you want to advance it to Basic is going
to depend on two things:

1.  How long you expect to keep wielding it?
   If you get your hands on another source of
   MR, would you want to trade up to a higher-
   damage weapon?  (You'd keep MB around
   for its engraving ability, of course, but that
   does not require wielding it.)  The answer is
   going to depend on play style as well as the
   details of your situation in the game.
   Personally, I would look for another source
   of MR and then seek a better weapon
   (Grayswandir, Excalibur, etc.), but some
   players value Magicbane's special effects
   (stunning and whatnot) more than damage.

2. Do you intend to use a stack of daggers
   as projectiles, either now or later?  If so,
   advancing dagger to Basic is useful even
   if you stop using Magicbane immediately
   after doing so.  My answer to this question
   (about daggers as projectiles) is usually
   yes, but again it depends on play style.
   Monks can potentially use attack spells
   instead, which frees up some inventory
   weight for other things.  So it's a choice.

HTH.HAND.


